   S3 — 5-Minute Revision Notes

      1. Object Storage

      S3 = AWS object storage service.
      Stores objects such as files, images, videos, logs, backups, etc.
      Objects are stored inside buckets.
      Object is identified using a key.

      2. Scalability & Durability

      Highly scalable; handles very large amounts of data and request traffic.
      Designed for extremely high durability.
      Data is redundantly stored across multiple facilities within an AWS Region.

      3. Storage Classes

      S3 Standard → frequent access, millisecond retrieval.
      Standard-IA → infrequent access, millisecond retrieval.
      Intelligent-Tiering → automatically moves data between access tiers.
      Glacier classes → archival data, lower storage cost, longer retrieval depending on class.

      4. Security & Access Control

      IAM policies
      Bucket policies
      Block Public Access
      ACLs
      Keep buckets private unless public access is specifically required.

      5. Encryption

      Encryption at rest.
      SSE-S3
      SSE-KMS
      Client-side encryption is also possible.

      6. Pre-signed URLs

      Temporary URL providing controlled access to an object.
      Client can directly upload/download from S3.
      Reduces backend bandwidth and processing load.

      7. Multipart Upload

      Split a large object into multiple parts.
      Upload parts independently/parallelly.
      Failed parts can be retried individually.
      Useful for large files.

      8. Versioning

      Keeps multiple versions of an object.
      Helps recover from accidental deletion or overwriting.

      9. Lifecycle Management

      Automatically transition objects between storage classes.
      Automatically expire/delete old objects.
      Example:
      Standard → Standard-IA → Glacier → Delete

      10. Replication

      Replicate objects between buckets.
      CRR → Cross-Region Replication.
      SRR → Same-Region Replication.

      11. Event Notifications

      S3 can generate events when objects are created/deleted.
      Can integrate with Lambda, SQS, SNS, etc.

      12. Static Website Hosting

      Can host static HTML/CSS/JavaScript content.

