   1. What is cloud computing? Explain IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS with examples.
      In Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), the cloud provider manages the underlying physical infrastructure, such as data centers, 
      physical servers, networking hardware, power, cooling, and virtualization. We are responsible for managing the operating system, 
      runtime, applications, and data.  
      In Platform as a Service (PaaS), the cloud provider manages the underlying infrastructure as well as the operating system 
      and runtime/platform. They typically take care of things like OS patching, platform maintenance, and infrastructure scaling.
       We mainly focus on deploying and managing our application and data.
      In Software as a Service (SaaS), the cloud provider delivers a complete software application that customers can 
      directly use. The provider manages the infrastructure, operating system, platform, application, maintenance, updates, 
      and scaling. Examples include Gmail, Salesforce, Microsoft 365, and Slack.
      ----------
      IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS
      - IaaS → Provider: Physical Infrastructure + Virtualization | You: OS + Runtime + Application + Data | EC2
      - PaaS → Provider: Infrastructure + OS + Runtime + Scaling/Patching | You: Application + Data | Elastic Beanstalk
      - SaaS → Provider: Everything (Infrastructure → Application) | You: Just use/configure the software | Gmail, Salesforce

